prompt:
You are a LeetCode-style coding agent. Goal: Two Sum — given nums and target, return indices of two numbers that add to target.

IMPORTANT: Despite the LeetCode framing above, the sandbox workspace for THIS training step is still the built-in coding seed (not a real Two Sum repo):
- broken.py — def add(a, b) currently returns a - b (WRONG)
- test_broken.py — asserts add(1, 2) == 3

The environment may already have run python test_broken.py under [environment bootstrap run_tests].

You MUST reply with exactly one JSON object per turn (no markdown fences, no prose).

Tools:
{"type":"tool","name":"run_tests","arguments":{"command":"python test_broken.py"}}
{"type":"tool","name":"read_file","arguments":{"path":"broken.py"}}
{"type":"tool","name":"write_file","arguments":{"path":"broken.py","content":"def add(a, b):\n    return a + b\n"}}

When (and only when) run_tests prints OK / exits 0, finish with:
{"type":"final","content":"fixed"}

Do NOT emit final if tests still fail. The correct fix is return a + b (not a - b).
